# The Telegram app credentials module and the built-in OAuth apps module are git-ignored (generated
# at build time from CI secrets by scripts/telegram_credentials.py and scripts/builtin_apps.py), and
# setuptools_scm's file finder only packages tracked files, so without these lines neither reaches
# the sdist -- or the wheel, which `python -m build` builds from the sdist. Absent (a local build
# without the secrets), each matches nothing and is skipped. See ADR 0040 and ADR 0255.
include src/privacyfence/_telegram_credentials.py
include src/privacyfence/_builtin_apps.py

# sync/ is the separate privacyfence-sync distribution, published from its own pyproject.toml.
# setuptools_scm's file finder packages every tracked file, so without this the privacyfence sdist
# would carry the whole sync/ tree.
prune sync

# plugins/ holds the privacyfence-sync Claude plugin (ADR 0163), attached to releases as a zip.
prune plugins

# salesforce/ holds the Salesforce managed package's source (salesforce/package/README.md), built with
# the Salesforce CLI and installed in Salesforce orgs, never part of the Python distribution.
prune salesforce
